  "claim_boundary": "Same-start M8 simulation comparison with continuous probe/search/insertion-to-CAD-bottom dynamics. The frozen P1v3 branch uses measured simulated F/T and tip-z for direction and support-state beliefs, then fuses a synthetic visual prior with soft approximate-CAD radial annuli. The CAD likelihood has a 0.35 mm transition width and a nonzero floor; it does not use the true center or MuJoCo contact points. A conservative posterior planner selects transport and residual coverage. Search-to-insertion handoff uses persistent tip-z progress and bounded observed wrench without true-center or MuJoCo contact tags; bottom uses CAD depth plus Fz. All branches share the same post-capture tip-RCC energy/CAD guard; it does not alter search. This is not hardware, random-distribution, or general-superiority evidence.",
